  <prompt>
    Persist the `paraId → legal-number` map BOTH in the projection payload (already emitted by 040) AND with the
    document session ledger, so it survives edits. Per R4, an edit keeps a paragraph's `paraId` stable; new/split
    paragraphs re-anchor per R4 — so the persisted map lets a reloaded session resolve `paraId → number` without a
    recompute divergence, and edited docs keep a stable `paraId → number` for unchanged paragraphs. This is FR-17
    (owner clarification: BOTH stores) and the persistence half of F-4 (stable reference). REUSE the R4 session-ledger
    persistence (ADR-040 session ledger) — do NOT invent a new store; the ledger already carries per-session document
    state and this map rides alongside it.
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer (BFF + Compose). Expert in the R4 session ledger (ADR-040), the `paraId`-anchored re-anchor layer (`ParaIdPreParser` / `AnnotationReanchorService` / `DocxAnnotationReader`), and the projection payload extended in 040. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>
    The `paraId → legal-number` map is persisted in TWO places: the projection payload (from 040) AND the R4 document
    session ledger. Reloading a session resolves the map without recompute divergence; an edited doc keeps a stable
    `paraId → number` for unchanged paragraphs (new/split paragraphs re-anchor per R4). A seam slice covers
    reload-resolves-map and edit-preserves-stable-mapping; the persistence reuses the existing session-ledger store
    (no new store introduced).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      WS-4's reference fields now ride on the projection payload (040), which is emitted per read. But the analysis/
      citation layer must resolve `paraId → number` for a session that has been reloaded or edited — after the
      projection was first built. R4's session ledger (ADR-040) already persists per-session document state, and R4
      keeps `paraId` stable across edits (new/split paragraphs re-anchor via `AnnotationReanchorService.cs:14-22`,
      doc-order-index hints in `DocxAnnotationReader` `:323-333`). This task persists the map alongside that ledger so
      the reference survives edits and reloads. Owner clarification (spec Owner Clarifications): the map persists in
      BOTH the projection payload AND the session ledger. Design §4 WS-4; spec FR-17. Line numbers are indicative —
      RE-GREP before editing.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs — persist the `paraId → legal-number` map into the R4 session ledger alongside existing per-session document state (`paraId` ×47 usage; reanchor by Levenshtein + position)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeDocxProjection.cs — the payload carrying the reference fields (040) that also feeds the ledger-persisted map</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/AnnotationReanchorService.cs — `paraId` re-anchor layer (`:14-22`): edits keep `paraId` stable, new/split re-anchor — the map must ride this stability</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationReader.cs — `ParagraphHint` = doc-order index (`:323-333`); the re-anchor input the map coexists with</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.claude/adr/ADR-040-session-ledger.md — the R4 session ledger this task reuses (do NOT invent a new store)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/seam/ — seam slice: reload-resolves-map + edit-preserves-stable-mapping (ADR-038)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="040" status="pending">The projection payload extended with `computedNumber`/`numberingLevel`/`listPath`/`headingLevel` — the source of the `paraId → legal-number` map this task also persists to the session ledger.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-17">The `paraId → legal-number` map MUST persist in BOTH the projection payload AND the document session ledger (owner clarification: BOTH). Scope: reloading a session resolves the map without recompute divergence; unchanged paragraphs keep a stable `paraId → number` across edits.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-040">REUSE the R4 session ledger for persistence — the map rides alongside the existing per-session document state. Scope: do NOT invent a new store, cache, table, or persistence surface; extend the ledger's existing session state (see escalation).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / §11">This is a modify-only extension of the existing session-ledger persistence + the 040 payload — no new component. Scope: if a new store appears necessary, that is a §11 new-surface event → STOP and surface (escalation), do not create silently.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">The projection + persistence stay `byte[]`-in / projection-out; no `Microsoft.Graph` type above `SpeFileStore`. Scope: map persistence happens inside `Services/Compose/` against the existing ledger.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">No AI-internal type injected into the persistence path — WS-4 exposes the reference map TO the analysis layer via the projection/ledger contract; it does NOT inject `IOpenAiClient`/executor into `Services/Compose/`. Scope: `Services/Compose/` stays pure (Tier-1 NetArchTest green).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Add/extend a seam slice for reload-resolves-map + edit-preserves-mapping at the KEEP path (`tests/integration/seam/`); NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration, or ctor-null tests. Scope: the seam exercises a real reload/edit round-trip through the ledger.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / BFF Hygiene §10">State the Placement Justification in the PR (cite `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`); measure compressed publish size and report absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (incl. PDBs) — expected ~0 MB. Scope: run `/conflict-check` before the PR.</constraint>
  </constraints>

