  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the FULL rigor-level declaration (🔒 RIGOR LEVEL: FULL / 📋 REASON / 📖 PROTOCOL STEPS). Load spec FR-17, design §4 WS-4, ADR-040 (session ledger), ADR-007/013/038, `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Confirm the ledger can carry the map">RE-GREP the R4 session-ledger persistence in `ComposeService.cs` and confirm the existing session state can carry the `paraId → legal-number` map WITHOUT a new store. If it cannot, STOP per the escalation trigger before writing any new persistence surface.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Persist to the projection payload">Confirm the map is present in the projection payload (from 040) — the immediate render/citation source. No new work if 040 already emits it; wire the ledger persistence from the same payload data.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Persist to the session ledger">Persist the `paraId → legal-number` map into the R4 session ledger alongside existing per-session document state, so it survives reloads and edits (unchanged paragraphs keep a stable `paraId → number`; new/split re-anchor per R4).</step>
    <step order="4" name="Checkpoint">Run `context-handoff` (silent: "✅ Checkpoint.").</step>
    <step order="5" name="Seam slice">Add/extend a seam slice (`tests/integration/seam/`): (a) reload a session → the map resolves without recompute divergence; (b) edit a doc → unchanged paragraphs keep a stable `paraId → number`, new/split re-anchor (ADR-038; no banned mock/DI/ctor tests).</step>
    <step order="6" name="Build + hygiene">Build BFF; run the Compose suite + new seam. Run `dotnet publish -c Release` and report compressed size + delta vs ~49.63 MB (incl. PDBs). Run `/conflict-check`. State the Placement Justification for the PR.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Set task ✅ in tasks/TASK-INDEX.md">Update `projects/spaarkeai-compose-fidelity-r4.5/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set task 041 status to ✅. Record any deviation in `projects/spaarkeai-compose-fidelity-r4.5/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If persisting the map with the session ledger would require a NEW store (cache, table, blob, or persistence surface) rather than extending R4's existing session state — STOP and surface per root CLAUDE.md §11 (new-surface justification) + §6.5 (ADR Conflict). Confirm the ledger can carry the map FIRST; do not create a new persistence surface silently.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs (map persisted to the R4 session ledger)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/ (reload-resolves-map + edit-preserves-mapping seam slice)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a projected document, when its projection is produced, then the `paraId → legal-number` map is present in BOTH the projection payload AND the persisted session ledger.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a persisted session, when it is reloaded, then the `paraId → legal-number` map resolves without a recompute divergence from the original projection.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an edited document, when unchanged paragraphs are inspected, then each keeps its stable `paraId → number`; new/split paragraphs re-anchor per R4 (not a silent number loss).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The persistence reuses the R4 session ledger — no new store, cache, table, or persistence surface is introduced (§11 / ADR-040); if one appeared necessary the escalation fired.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the persistence path does NOT inject any AI-internal type into `Services/Compose/` and does NOT reach `Microsoft.Graph` above `SpeFileStore` — Tier-1 NetArchTest stays green (ADR-007/013).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A seam slice at the `tests/integration/seam/` KEEP path exercises reload + edit round-trips through the ledger; no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`/DI-registration/ctor-null test is added (ADR-038).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF build + Compose suite green; compressed publish size reported with ~0 MB delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (≤60 MB ceiling); `/conflict-check` clean.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">TASK-INDEX.md shows task 041 as ✅ and any deviation is recorded in projects/spaarkeai-compose-fidelity-r4.5/notes/.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Spec FR-17; design §4 WS-4; owner clarification = BOTH stores. This is the persistence half of the reference
    layer — 040 added the payload fields, 042 builds the citation resolver on top. The map's edit-survival rides on
    R4's `paraId` stability (`AnnotationReanchorService`); this task does NOT change the re-anchor algorithm, only
    persists the number map alongside it.
  </notes>

